=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  helpers.tsx is a PURE UTILITY module (75 lines, six exported helpers, no JSX UI, no
  data hooks, no i18n keys). The real parity value is the ported core (consumed by the
  other native status surfaces exactly as the web status components import these
  helpers); the surface presents that core as a reference panel honouring the P4 leaf
  contract, since the prompt's uniform "feature view" template requires a rendered
  surface with all states.

  Web export                 → Native port (helpers.Adapter.swift)
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  getStatusColor(status)     → StatusHelpers.kind(for:) → StatusKind.tone (ADR-006:
                               web #22c55e/#f59e0b/#ef4444/#6b7280 → statusSuccess/
                               statusWarning/statusDanger/neutral semantic tokens).
  statusTextClass(status)    → folded into the same tone (the foreground colour).
  getStatusIcon(status)      → StatusHelpers.symbolName(for:) (CheckCircle→
                               checkmark.circle.fill, AlertTriangle→
                               exclamationmark.triangle.fill, XCircle→
                               xmark.circle.fill; default→triangle, as the web).
  formatUptime(seconds)      → StatusFormat.formatUptime (floor d/h/m, Xd Yh Zm /
                               Yh Zm / Zm — verbatim integer wording).
  formatBytes(bytes)         → StatusFormat.formatBytes (1024 ladder B/KB/MB/GB/TB,
                               fmtNumber(v,1) via locale NumberFormatter, 0→"0 B").
  statusToBadgeVariant(...)  → StatusHelpers.badgeKind(for:) → TSTone (success/
                               warning/danger/neutral).

  FAITHFUL DIVERGENCE (no silent drift, Honesty rule 9): the web success set for
  getStatusColor/statusTextClass/getStatusIcon INCLUDES "connected", but
  statusToBadgeVariant's success set does NOT. So "connected" renders the green check
  glyph yet a NEUTRAL badge. Reproduced via two classifications (kind vs badgeKind)
  and pinned by StatusBadgeKindTests.testConnectedIsSuccessForColourButNeutralForBadge.

